// Title: Python Path Configuration File Creation - MacOS
// Sigma ID: 4f394635-13ef-4599-b677-3353e0f84f55
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Andreas Braathen (mnemonic.io)
// Date: 2024-04-25 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.006
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects creation of a Python path configuration file (.pth) in Python library folders, which can
//   be maliciously abused for code execution and persistence. Modules referenced by these files are
//   run at every Python startup (v3.5+), regardless of whether the module is imported by the calling
//   script. Default paths are '\lib\site-packages\*.pth' (Windows) and '/lib/pythonX.Y/site-
//   packages/*.pth' (Unix and macOS).
// False positives:
//   - Although .pth files are discouraged due to potential security implications, these are legitimate files by specification.
// References:
//   - https://www.volexity.com/blog/2024/04/12/zero-day-exploitation-of-unauthenticated-remote-code-execution-vulnerability-in-globalprotect-cve-2024-3400/
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3de2a4392b8715bad070b2ae12243f166ead37830f7c6d24e778985927f9caac
//   - https://docs.python.org/3/library/site.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules-threat-hunting/macos/file/file_event/file_event_macos_python_path_configuration_files.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath matches regex "(?i)/lib/python3\\.([5-9]|[0-9]{2})/site-packages/" and FolderPath endswith ".pth"
